# Kaiser Jagdstandbild (Bad Ischl, 1910): the old emperor in hunting dress
# (hat with a chamois-beard tuft t, patinated Joppe t/T, Lederhosen O/l,
# knee socks t/T, boots l), a rifle l slung over his shoulder, all bronze
# O/l with t patina, k outline (front layer). He stands on a rough-hewn
# stone block (i lit left face, m mid face, d shadowed right face, d chisel
# cracks, a blank bronze plaque O/o/l: no text). Drawn = solid (D-038):
# the block is sprite rows 16..47 = the 2x2 stone tiles (rows 13-14); its k
# top edge is row 16, 32 px above the street, an i lip on row 17.
# Pigeon seat: the hat crown's top, pixels (14..18, 0), centred on the
# origin column x 16, 48 px above the street (16 px above the block).
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grid is the source.
sprite = kaiser_jagdstandbild
size   = 32x48
origin = 16,48
anim   = idle frames=1
